license: AGPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Synthetic, stdlib-only Python toy: 128 seeded neurons in two ellipses,
  four stored wave fields, a one-shot outer-product associative memory
  and a frozen refusal gate. It is not a brain, not neuroscience and not
  a medical or clinical tool. The repository documents measured behaviour
  and limits, including negative results. v0.2.0 adds an 808 nm
  light-dose coupling: a hormetic ATP proxy lowers effective probe
  noise, mitochondrial stress raises it, and light before stress onset
  protects recall more than the same light after onset. The light
  claims are pre-registered and measured in results/results_light.json.
keywords:
  - "synthetic"
  - "toy-model"
  - "associative-memory"
  - "reproducible"
  - "photobiomodulation"
  - "python"
